# garmin-mcp env file template (garmin design section 5; deploy/README.md).
# Copy to /home/mcp/env/garmin.env (0600, owned by mcp) and fill the values
# as Maciek: never commit filled values. MCP_BEARER is a generated hex value
# (openssl rand -hex 32). GARMIN_API_KEY is the Garmin Connect Personal API
# key created in Garmin Connect web (expiry 365 days); the server code reads
# this name. MCP_HOST/MCP_PORT stay as templated.
# Values go in bare: no quotes, no placeholder text. A quoted or placeholder value yields HTTP 401 at the Personal API token exchange (verified Nov 8 2026).
MCP_BEARER=
GARMIN_API_KEY=
MCP_HOST=0.0.0.0
MCP_PORT=8017

# --- Garmin local archive (garmin-local-archive-design-final.md Rev 7) -----
# Two non-credential knobs plus three sync-tuning knobs, all optional. With
# everything unset the server behaves exactly as before this feature: live
# reads only, no background sync, no store (the PR alone changes nothing).
#
# GARMIN_STORE_DIR: the on-box archive store, bind-mounted into the
#   container (OD-2: /home/mcp/garmin-store, 0700, owned by mcp).
# GARMIN_STORE_MODE: off | live_only | read_through. Default when the dir is
#   set but the mode is unset: off. live_only mounts the store for the sync
#   while reads stay live (the deploy flow and the rebuild flow, §5.4);
#   read_through serves reads from the store with a live fallback and is
#   rejected at startup unless the store's init checks pass (§5.1).
# GARMIN_SYNC_MAX_CALLS: per-run upstream-call hard cap (default 1500; §4.3).
# GARMIN_SYNC_PACING_S: minimum seconds between two upstream sync calls
#   (default 2; §4.3).
# GARMIN_SYNC_HOURLY: 1 enables the hourly refresher tier (:43). OFF until
#   the phase-5 trial verdict — adoption decisions M1/OD-3. Leave unset.
#GARMIN_STORE_DIR=/home/mcp/garmin-store
#GARMIN_STORE_MODE=live_only
#GARMIN_SYNC_MAX_CALLS=1500
#GARMIN_SYNC_PACING_S=2
#GARMIN_SYNC_HOURLY=0
